{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1920794","formula":"Na(Li₁.₅Al₁.₅)Al₆(Si₆O₁₈)(BO₃)₃(OH)₃(OH)","hill":"Al7.5B3H4Li1.5NaO31Si6","elements":["H","Li","B","O","Na","Al","Si"],"composition":{"B":3.0,"H":4.0,"O":31.0,"Al":7.5,"Li":1.5,"Na":1.0,"Si":6.0},"names":{"en":"Elbaite","ru":"Эльбаит","uk":"Ельбаїт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Elbaite, a sodium, lithium, aluminium boro-silicate, with the chemical composition Na(Li1.5Al1.5)Al6Si6O18(BO3)3(OH)4, is a mineral species belonging to the six-member ring cyclosilicate tourmaline group. Elbaite forms three series, with dravite, with fluor-liddicoatite, and with schorl. Due to these series, specimens with the ideal endmember formula are not found occurring naturally.","ru":"Эльбаит — минерал из класса силикатов (кольцевых силикатов), название получил по месту находки на острове Эльба (Италия). Относится к группе турмалинов. Проявляет пьезоэлектрические и пироэлектрические свойства.","uk":"Ельбаїт — мінерал, літіїстий різновид турмаліну."},"fame":23,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1920794","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbaite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%AD%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%95%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%97%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elbaite_with_albite_-_S%C3%A3o_Jos%C3%A9_da_Safira,_Minas_Gerais,_Brazil.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id"